The project titled "CosmetriScan: Visual Analysis of Chemical Usage in Cosmetic Products" was developed to unravel the complexities of cosmetic product formulations by delivering clear, visual insights into chemical usage patterns, safety risks, and brand formulation diversity. Leveraging Python’s data analytics and visualization libraries such as Pandas, Matplotlib, and Seaborn, the project transformed a rich dataset of cosmetic ingredients into a series of compelling and interactive visualizations.
Through structured objectives and targeted data cleaning, this project enabled users to explore and evaluate multiple aspects of cosmetic chemistry with ease and precision. Key outcomes of the project include:
•	Identification of the most frequently used chemicals across the dataset, spotlighting commonly recurring ingredients and their regulatory relevance.
•	Category-wise chemical usage analysis, providing insights into how different cosmetic product types vary in formulation complexity and concentration.
•	Brand vs. Chemical Risk Mapping, revealing formulation strategies and highlighting potential consumer exposure to high-risk chemicals by brand.
•	Diversity of chemical use, explored through time-series line graphs to track trends and variability in formulation practices.
•	Correlation between chemical count and product longevity, helping assess whether ingredient diversity impacts shelf life or performance.
•	Outlier management through the capping method, ensuring cleaner, more reliable data analysis and minimizing the effect of extreme values.
With consistent formatting, purposeful graph selection, and a focus on user clarity, this project serves as a valuable tool for regulatory agencies, cosmetic brands, researchers, and conscious consumers alike. It supports data-driven decision-making in product development, safety evaluation, and sustainable formulation practices.
The methodology is scalable and can be enhanced further by incorporating toxicology datasets, ingredient sourcing data, or consumer feedback metrics. With increasing emphasis on clean beauty and transparency, this dashboard acts as a foundation for responsible innovation in the cosmetic industry.
